 {
  "url": "about.html",
  "type": "About",
  "title": "Welcome to Sam's Table",
  "desc": "Meet Sam, a culinary student in Las Vegas who loves home cooking, meal prep, and trying new food while traveling.",
  "text": "About Welcome to Sam's Table Hi, I'm Sam! I'm a culinary student in Las Vegas, and Sam's Table is where I keep everything I love about food in one place: recipes I've saved, dishes I've made at home and in class, and the restaurants that are worth the trip. Life gets busy, and it's easy to just stop at a drive-through. But making food doesn't have to be hard or expensive. Cooking at home or meal prepping for the week tastes so much better, and you know exactly what's going into your food. Even on my busiest days, I make time for good food. Food is my love language, and love is my secret ingredient. I also love to travel, and trying new food is half the reason I go. Closer to home, I've traveled to Mexico, Canada, and Alaska. My adventures have also taken me across Europe, from Stockholm and Visby in Sweden to Helsinki, Kotka, and Hamina in Finland. I've explored the Baltics in Tallinn, Riga, and Klaipeda, plus Gdynia in Poland, Copenhagen in Denmark, and Berlin and Hamburg in Germany. Farther south, I've eaten my way through Zadar and Dubrovnik in Croatia, Corfu, Santorini, Mykonos, and Athens in Greece, Istanbul in Turkey, and Trieste in Italy. Here you'll find simple, budget-friendly recipes I've actually tested, meal prep ideas, notes from culinary school, and honest, detailed reviews from my travels and closer to home. Every recipe here is one I've tried and collected over the years, from family favorites to YouTube finds, Reddit posts, and dishes from culinary school. Pull up a chair. There's always room at the table."
 }
